[{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions require the use of Double Angle Formulae, Reversing the Chain rule, Integration by Parts and Integration by Substitution</strong></p><p>Find the exact mean value of each of the following on the given intervals:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\pi x\\cos(\\pi x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left[0,\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\operatorname{cosec}^2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left[\\frac\\pi4,\\frac\\pi3\\right]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{x^2}{5x^3+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,1]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin^2 4x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left[0,\\frac\\pi4\\right]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=2^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[2,5]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin 2x\\cos^3 2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left[0,\\frac\\pi{12}\\right]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The mean value on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[a,b]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{b-a}\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2/2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt2/2}\\pi x\\cos(\\pi x^2)\\,dx\n=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2/2}\\left[\\frac12\\sin(\\pi x^2)\\right]_0^{\\sqrt2/2}\n=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{1}{\\pi/3-\\pi/4}\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/3}\\cosec^2x\\,dx\n=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left[-\\cot x\\right]_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/3}\n=\\frac{12-4\\sqrt3}{\\pi}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^1\\frac{x^2}{5x^3+1}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac1{15}\\ln|5x^3+1|\\right]_0^1\n=\\frac1{15}\\ln6.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The interval has length 1, so the mean value is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{15}\\ln6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin^2A=\\frac12(1-\\cos2A)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{4}{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sin^24x\\,dx\n =\\frac4\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\frac12(1-\\cos8x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac4\\pi\\left[\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\sin8x}{16}\\right]_0^{\\pi/4}=\\frac12.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac13\\int_2^5 2^x\\,dx\n=\\frac{1}{3\\ln2}\\left[2^x\\right]_2^5\n=\\frac{28}{3\\ln2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\pi/12}\\sin2x\\cos^32x\\,dx\n=\\frac{12}{\\pi}\\left[-\\frac18\\cos^42x\\right]_0^{\\pi/12}\n=\\frac{21}{32\\pi}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Find the mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{e^{-3x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The worked solution uses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=xe^{-3x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Integration by parts gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int xe^{-3x}\\,dx=-\\frac{x}{3}e^{-3x}-\\frac19e^{-3x}+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore the mean value as worked in the source solutions is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1a\\int_0^a xe^{-3x}\\,dx=\\frac{1-(3a+1)e^{-3a}}{9a}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}}+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,8]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant is 2. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac18\\int_0^8\\left(\\frac2{\\sqrt{3x+1}}+k\\right)dx\n=\\frac18\\left[\\frac43\\sqrt{3x+1}+kx\\right]_0^8\n=\\frac23+k.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since this mean value is 2, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac43\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,3]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is half the mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)=\\frac37x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,k]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive number. Find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac13\\int_0^3\\sqrt{x+1}\\,dx\n=\\frac13\\left[\\frac23(x+1)^{3/2}\\right]_0^3=\\frac{14}{9}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,k]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1k\\int_0^k\\frac37x^2\\,dx=\\frac{k^2}{7}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{14}{9}=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac{k^2}{7}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^2=\\frac{196}{9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is positive, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{14}{3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The velocity of a car after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=\\dfrac{30t}{t+5}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres per second.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the mean velocity for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"17.9\\text{ m s}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to 3 significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Use the mean value theorem to calculate the mean acceleration of the car for the same time interval.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1{20}\\int_0^{20}\\frac{30t}{t+5}\\,dt\n=\\frac1{20}\\left[30t-150\\ln|t+5|\\right]_0^{20}\n=17.9\\text{ m s}^{-1}\\quad(3\\text{ s.f.}).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\na=\\frac{dv}{dt}=\\frac{150}{(t+5)^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore the mean acceleration on the interval is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1{20}\\int_0^{20}\\frac{150}{(t+5)^2}\\,dt\n=\\frac{15}{2}\\left[-(t+5)^{-1}\\right]_0^{20}\n=1.2\\text{ m s}^{-2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Given that the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq x\\leq4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <strong>a)</strong> Find the mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Another function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)=f(x)+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq x\\leq4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>b)</strong> Given that the mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac43\\ln4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, state the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac13\\int_1^4\\ln x\\,dx\n=\\frac13[x\\ln x-x]_1^4\n=\\frac43\\ln4-1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Adding a constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to a function adds <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to its mean value. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac43\\ln4-1+c=\\frac43\\ln4,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with shaded regions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> enclosed by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The areas <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are equal.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.34/questions/assets/FMQ_2.34_question7_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The signed area between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\pi/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is zero because the two shaded areas are equal. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{\\pi/2}(\\sin x-k)\\,dx=0,\n\\qquad 1-\\frac{k\\pi}{2}=0,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The root mean square (RMS) of a function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> defined for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\leq x\\leq b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> over this interval is</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b[f(x)]^2\\,dx}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Find the RMS of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=4\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in exact form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\operatorname{RMS}(f)=\\sqrt{\\frac1{2\\pi}\\int_0^{2\\pi}16\\cos^2x\\,dx}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^2x=\\frac12(1+\\cos2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^{2\\pi}16\\cos^2x\\,dx=8\\left[x+\\frac12\\sin2x\\right]_0^{2\\pi}=16\\pi.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\operatorname{RMS}(f)=\\sqrt8=2\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q9","number":9,"question":"<p><strong>a)</strong> Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^4\\theta=\\frac18(3+4\\cos2\\theta+\\cos4\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In a mechanical system, the velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\text{ m s}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a vibrating component at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=a\\cos^2(kt)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants. The effective speed of the component over one complete cycle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is defined to be the square root of the mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> over this time interval. <strong>b)</strong> Show that the effective speed of the component is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sqrt3a}{2\\sqrt2}\\text{ m s}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Question 10: Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^2A=\\frac12(1+\\cos2A)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\cos^4\\theta =\\frac14(1+2\\cos2\\theta+\\cos^22\\theta)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac14\\left(1+2\\cos2\\theta+\\frac12(1+\\cos4\\theta)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac18(3+4\\cos2\\theta+\\cos4\\theta).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Here <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=a^2\\cos^4(kt)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> over one cycle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,\\pi/k]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{k}{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\pi/k}a^2\\cos^4(kt)\\,dt\n =\\frac{a^2k}{8\\pi}\\int_0^{\\pi/k}(3+4\\cos2kt+\\cos4kt)\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{3a^2}{8}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The effective speed is therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{3a^2/8}=\\frac{\\sqrt3a}{2\\sqrt2}\\text{ m s}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>For each of the following functions, defined over the domain <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-k\\pi\\leq x\\leq k\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for positive integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[f(x)]^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sinh(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an odd positive integer.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh(ix)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an odd positive integer.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sinh(ix)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an odd positive integer.</p></li></ol><p><strong>The following questions require the use of A-Level Further Maths Integration techniques</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sinh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an odd function and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\sinh x)^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd. Its integral over the symmetric interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[-k\\pi,k\\pi]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is zero, so its mean value is 0.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\cosh(ix)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}2=\\cos x.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\cos x)^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even, and its integral over <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[-k\\pi,k\\pi]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\int_0^{k\\pi}\\cos^n x\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. However, for odd <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> this integral is not generally zero over <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,k\\pi]\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; evaluating it gives For odd <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^n x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has opposite values at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so its integral over each interval of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is zero. Thus its mean value is 0.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sinh(ix)=i\\sin x.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For odd <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(i\\sin x)^n=i^n\\sin^n x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an odd function of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Its integral over <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[-k\\pi,k\\pi]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is zero, so its mean value is 0.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Find the exact mean value of each of the following for the given intervals:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{9+x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,3]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left[0,\\frac14\\right]\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x^2+7}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,a]\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for positive constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Questions 12--15: Calculus of Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac13\\int_0^3\\frac{1}{9+x^2}\\,dx\n=\\frac13\\left[\\frac13\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\right]_0^3\n=\\frac\\pi{36}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4\\int_0^{1/4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}\\,dx\n=4\\left[\\frac12\\arcsin(2x)\\right]_0^{1/4}=\\frac\\pi3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1a\\int_0^a\\frac{1}{x^2+7}\\,dx\n=\\frac{1}{a\\sqrt7}\\left[\\arctan\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt7}\\right)\\right]_0^a\n=\\frac{1}{a\\sqrt7}\\arctan\\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt7}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Find the exact mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-6x+16}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Completing the square, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-6x+16=7+(x-3)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac16\\int_0^6\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-6x+16}}\\,dx\n =\\frac16\\left[\\ln\\left(x-3+\\sqrt{7+(x-3)^2}\\right)\\right]_0^6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac16\\ln7.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Find the mean value of the function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-9}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\leq x\\leq a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in exact logarithmic form.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1{a-3}\\int_3^a\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-9}}\\,dx\n=\\frac{1}{a-3}\\left[\\ln\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2-9}\\right)\\right]_3^a\n=\\frac{1}{a-3}\\ln\\left(\\frac{a+\\sqrt{a^2-9}}{3}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The intensity of a signal, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I\" data-display=\"false\"></span> watts per square metre, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours after a transmitter is switched on is modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nI=12+8\\sech^2(0.5t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the mean signal intensity during the first four hours after the transmitter is switched on, giving your answer correct to three significant figures.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac14\\int_0^4\\left(12+8\\sech^2(0.5t)\\right)dt\n=\\frac14[12t+16\\tanh(0.5t)]_0^4\n=12+4\\tanh2=15.9\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>to three significant figures, in watts per square metre.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>The brightness of a light-emitting diode, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in lumens, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> minutes after it is switched on, is modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nB=50+20\\cosech^2(0.2t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the mean brightness of the LED during the second minute after it is switched on, giving your answer to three significant figures.</p>","steps":["<p>The second minute is the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq t\\leq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_1^2\\left(50+20\\cosech^2(0.2t)\\right)dt\n =[50t-100\\coth(0.2t)]_1^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =50-100\\coth(0.4)+100\\coth(0.2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx293\\text{ lumens}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The interval has length 1, so this is the mean brightness to three significant figures.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>The velocity of a cyclist after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nv=\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{t^2+9}}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>metres per second for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the mean velocity of the cyclist for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3.14\\text{ m s}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Use the mean value theorem to calculate the mean acceleration of the cyclist for the same time interval giving your answer to three significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1{12}\\int_0^{12}\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{t^2+9}}\\,dt\n=\\frac{18}{12}\\left[\\ln\\left(t+\\sqrt{t^2+9}\\right)\\right]_0^{12}\n=\\frac32\\ln(4+\\sqrt{17})=3.14\\text{ m s}^{-1}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>to three significant figures.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The mean acceleration is the change in velocity divided by the time interval:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{v(12)-v(0)}{12}\n=\\frac{6/\\sqrt{17}-6}{12}\n\\approx-0.379\\text{ m s}^{-2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus the mean deceleration is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.379\\text{ m s}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=\\frac a5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the mean value of the function</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-x^2}}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p+q\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Question 18: A-Level Further Maths Partial Fractions</strong></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac1a\\int_0^a\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-x^2}}\\,dx\n=\\frac1a\\left[\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)\\right]_0^a\n=\\frac1a\\arcsin\\left(\\frac a5\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=a/5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq\\pi/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arcsin(a/5)=\\pi/2-\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The mean value is therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2a}-\\frac{\\theta}{a}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.34-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows part of the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nf(x)=\\frac{x+2}{(x^2+2)(x-1)}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>with shaded regions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> enclosed by the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac52\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.34/questions/assets/FMQ_2.34_question18_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The areas <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are equal. Determine the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Write</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{x+2}{(x^2+2)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{Bx+C}{x^2+2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Equating coefficients gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nf(x)=\\frac1{x-1}-\\frac{x}{x^2+2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The signed area from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=5/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_{3/2}^{5/2}f(x)\\,dx\n =\\left[\\ln|x-1|-\\frac12\\ln(x^2+2)\\right]_{3/2}^{5/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{561}}{11}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The two areas are equal, so this signed area is zero after subtracting the rectangle of height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and width 1. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nk=\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{561}}{11}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]